// ============================================================
// Succy_Load.js — Succy Load Image & Resize as GLUE, NodeStructure v0.3 (D-156)
// Two ways in (Image: one picture + a mask you draw · Folder: the pictures of a folder), then ONE resize for picture and mask.
// What it outputs reaches every Succy node on its wires LIVE, no Queue (the Python flags it: SUCCY_LIVE).
// This file contains ONLY: spec (catalog pieces), config and the natives it hides. Zero DOM, zero CSS, zero timers.
//   Image | Folder (top bar) ..................................................... `segmented_element` on `$native.mode`
//   the picture you draw on, zoom / pan ............................................ `view_box` + `$live.shot_system` (or the live `image` input)
//   the box, the free hand mask, the mask tinted on the picture .................... `marquee_element` · `brush_element` · `veil_element` inside
//   drop / paste (Ctrl+V) / 📂 a picture, no Queue ................................ `load_mask` + `drop_element` (native upload, name in `source`)
//   Result: what leaves the node, resized, live (Folder shows it always) ........... `$live.live_system.self.image` (live_system `self`)
//   the folder: path, Next / Index, the strip of thumbnails, ↺ ...................... `field_element` · `segmented_element` · `strip_element`
//   Resize Off / Custom / Scale · fit · anchor 3×3 · pad colour · Outpaint ......... `segmented_element` / `slider_element` on the natives
//   EXT on Index / Width / Height: the slider steps aside, a real input with a chip . `ext_node` (mode chip) + `chip_input`
//   the measures line: picture · out (where, how big) ............................... local `say` (util/mask-math.js resizePlan = the Python's)
//   what the picture still needs (a Run, a source with nothing yet) ................. `$live.ready_system` + `wait_element`
//   every input and output .......................................................... `chip_input` / `chip_output`
// Backend: Succy_Load/Succy_Load.py. Natives stay REAL (Python validates them) — only hidden; the controls below drive them.
// ============================================================
